---
export const title = 'Accessibility';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  The timeline is a table named by the days it shows. Each resource is a row, with its title as the row header and its
  events in its one cell. Events are buttons, named with their title, resource and time, that fire
  <code>event-click</code> on a click, <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd>. With <code>events-readonly</code> they are
  notes that cannot be focused. With <code>group-by</code>, each group's header row has its name as the row header and
  a button that says whether it expands or collapses the group (<code>aria-expanded</code>); the rows of a collapsed
  group are not in the table.
</p>

<p>
  Moves, resizes and new events are announced in a live region. On touch screens, people hold an event briefly before
  dragging it, so a swipe still scrolls the timeline, and <kbd>Escape</kbd> cancels a drag. Clicking empty time adds an
  event without dragging. Dragging needs a pointer, so also let people change an event's time and resource another way,
  such as in the dialog you open on <code>event-click</code>. Right-to-left layouts run the time axis from the right.
</p>
